    "result_text": "`BUILD SUCCESS`, test green. Here's how I addressed the review:\n\n## What I changed\n\n**#1 \u2014 Duplicated country-code knowledge (agreed, fixed).** This was the real problem. I created `TelephoneFormatter` in the `model` (domain) layer as the *single* owner of the `NATIONAL_LENGTHS` table. Both directions now route through it:\n- the inbound normalizer `OwnerTelephone.toE164(...)` calls `TelephoneFormatter.hasValidNationalLength(...)` (its own table and the duplicate method are gone);\n- the outbound display calls `TelephoneFormatter.toDisplay(...)`.\n\nAdding or changing a country is now a one-line edit in one place that updates both directions \u2014 no silent drift.\n\n**#3 \u2014 Inline grouping utility (agreed, fixed).** The \"group in threes\" loop is now a private `groupInThrees` helper inside `TelephoneFormatter`, not inline code.\n\n**#2 \u2014 Presentation logic on the entity (partially disagreed, but tidied).** I kept `telephoneDisplay` as an entity getter rather than moving derivation to the mapper/responder, and here's why: *every* other derived response field in this codebase \u2014 `displayName`, `initials`, `ageBand`, `locality`, `checkDigit`, `membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey` \u2014 is an `Owner`/`Person` getter that MapStruct reads by name. Making `telephoneDisplay` the lone field derived elsewhere would be *less* consistent, not more, and would split a uniform convention. (AGENTS.md's \"DTOs at the edges\" is about DTO-vs-entity flow through the pipeline steps, which is unchanged \u2014 DTOs still only appear at the first and last steps.)\n\nThat said, I took the legitimate part of the concern: `Owner.getTelephoneDisplay()` is now a one-line delegation to `TelephoneFormatter`, so the entity no longer carries the country-code table or the formatting mechanics \u2014 just a thin accessor like its siblings.\n\nI also chose `model` as the formatter's home (not inside `OwnerTelephone`) deliberately: putting it in `OwnerTelephone` would have forced the `Owner` entity to depend on the `rest.function.owner` (request-handling) package \u2014 a backwards dependency. In `model`, the dependencies stay correct: `model \u2192 model`, and `rest.function.owner \u2192 model`.\n\nNo mapper or OpenAPI change was needed \u2014 `telephoneDisplay` still maps automatically by getter name, and the acceptance test (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`, raw `telephone` unchanged) still passes.",
