    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe method works as a self-contained unit, but it places logic in the wrong unit and duplicates domain knowledge that already lives elsewhere.\n\n**1. Country-code knowledge is duplicated (the strongest issue).** `TELEPHONE_NATIONAL_LENGTHS` is, by its own Javadoc, a mirror: *\"Mirrors the country codes recognized at creation (see the telephone normalizer).\"* The set of valid country codes and their national-number lengths is a single domain fact that now has two sources of truth. A maintainer who adds a country to the normalizer (or changes a length) will silently produce un-formatted output here, because nothing links the two tables. The parsing/length knowledge should live in one place and be shared \u2014 ideally the same component that already normalizes to E.164 on the way in should own the inverse (split/group) on the way out.\n\n**2. Presentation formatting is accreting onto the persistence entity.** `Owner` is a JPA model entity. Giving it the digit-grouping/display-formatting logic turns it into a catch-all that mixes \"what is stored\" with \"how it is shown to humans.\" The codebase's own conventions (AGENTS.md: \"Keep DTOs at the edges \u2014 response DTO out at the responder\") point the other way: `telephoneDisplay` is a derived, response-only field (it's `readOnly` and \"Derived per response\" per the OpenAPI doc), so deriving it belongs with the response mapping / a dedicated telephone formatter, not on the entity. Co-locating it with the existing normalizer would also naturally resolve finding #1.\n\n**3. The grouping loop is a generic string utility embedded inline.** The \"group national digits in threes\" loop is reusable formatting mechanics with no dependency on `Owner`. If the formatting responsibility moves to a formatter/normalizer unit (per #2), this becomes a small private helper there rather than inline entity code.\n\nSuggested shape: move both the country-code table and the format logic into the existing telephone normalizer (or a sibling `TelephoneFormatter`), expose a `format(e164)` method, and have the responder/DTO call it to populate `telephoneDisplay`. That removes the duplicated table, keeps the entity free of presentation concerns, and keeps the inbound/outbound telephone knowledge together.",
